      "message": "Nit: I haven\u0027t analyzed the code carefully, but in general it would good if the stride, rows, and cols parameters are either all signed or all unsigned.\n\nIt is often convenient to declare the stride as signed so that we can go backward,\n\nIf the stride is unsigned, then we should cast it to `size_t` instead of `ptrdiff_t` before multiplying it with `r` to avoid potential overflow. (`size_t` is unsigned, `ptrdiff_t` is signed.)",
